    "conclusion": "The instrumentation itself left the 118.065 messages/second mean within 0.14% of the v126/v127 diagnostic mean. Both runs failed the unchanged stability gate, so no throughput qualification is made. Transaction commit is the largest intent worker substage, but PostgreSQL fsync and synchronous_commit remain required. Insert plus the full identity read account for another 10.336 ms per worker transaction. The next bounded hypothesis is to validate newly inserted rows from INSERT RETURNING while issuing the separate identity SELECT only for conflict or replay rows. This preserves full durable identity validation and unknown-commit reconciliation while removing one normal-path SQL exchange."
